 ### t-distribution truncation for splatting
-A projection truncation technique that replaces the fixed three-sigma rule used in vanilla 3DGS with a $\nu$-dependent critical value interpolation to handle fat-tailed Student's t-distributions. For t-distributions with thin tails (high $\nu$), the standard three-sigma rule is applied directly. For fat-tailed distributions (low $\nu$), critical values for different $\nu$ degrees are interpolated to compute the appropriate truncation threshold. Using a fixed three-sigma threshold on fat-tailed t-distributions causes excessive truncation or leakage, which interpolation resolves [S7].
